      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p><strong>Chennai to Mumbai packers and movers</strong> must navigate a complex web of statutory transit paperwork to ensure a smooth, compliant relocation. The first requirement is the <strong>GST e‑Way bill</strong>, an electronic document that authorises the movement of goods across state borders.</p>
<p>For a home shifting service in Chennai near Thiruvottiyur, the e‑Way bill is generated before the cargo leaves the city, capturing the GST value and ensuring tax compliance on the entire shipment from Chennai to Mumbai.</p>

<p>Next, the <strong>IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt (LR/Bilty)</strong> serves as the primary proof of transport. This receipt, issued by the Indian Bureau of Road Transport (IBR), records the cargo details, vehicle number, and the parties involved.</p>
<p>It is essential for both the <strong>mumbai to chennai distance by car</strong> calculation and for any dispute resolution, providing a verifiable trail that the goods were handled by licensed packers and movers.</p>

<p>To protect the cargo against unforeseen events, a <strong>100 % declared‑value IRDAI marine transit insurance</strong> is mandatory for high‑value items. This comprehensive policy covers accidental collision, fire, theft, and even delays caused by adverse weather or logistical hiccups.</p>
<p>The coverage is tailored to the declared value of the goods, offering peace of mind to customers seeking <strong>house shifting services in Chennai</strong> or <strong>house shifting services in Mumbai</strong>.</p>

